==Danish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|da|gmq-oda|tisdagh}}, from {{der|da|non|týsdagr|tý(r)sdagr}}. from {{der|da|gmw-pro|*Tīwas dag}}, cognate with {{cog|en|Tuesday}}. 

A compound of {{der|da|gem-pro|*Tīwaz|t=[[Tyr]]}} + {{m|gem-pro|*dagaz|t=day}}, a calque of {{der|da|la|diēs Mārtis|lit=day of Mars}}, which is itself a calque of {{der|da|grc|ἡμέρα Ἄρεως|lit=day of Ares}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|da|/ˈtiɐ̯ˀsda/|[ˈtsʰiɒ̯̽ˀsd̥æ]}}
* {{rhymes|da|a}}

